{"title":"1975 AHSME Problems/Problem 26","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_26\">Problem 26</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 26\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In acute <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> the bisector of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/a/23a32703170ad47915e2759411a096ec29abd060.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\measuredangle A$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"26\" height=\"13\" /> meets side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/5/6c52a41dcbd739f1d026c5d4f181438b75b76976.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. The circle with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/f/89fff82bb65d0215e49c8c91cb7c553da52205e2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> \nintersects side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />; and the circle with center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/4/0948661e822f2a953c43a57ac9e40b2734476de4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"32\" height=\"14\" /> intersects side <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/1/7/a179ff2638e4799cadd820db205c2beff6299ce9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/9/fc97ef67268cd4e91bacdf12b8901d7036c9a056.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$N$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Then it is always true that\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/d/32d8108600852fcac6b08a710decf998c3a808b4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\measuredangle CND+\\measuredangle BMD-\\measuredangle DAC =120^{\\circ} \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ AMDN\\ \\text{is a trapezoid}\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ BC\\ \\text{is parallel to}\\ MN\\\\ \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ AM-AN=\\frac{3(DB-DC)}{2}\\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ AB-AC=\\frac{3(DB-DC)}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"787\" height=\"57\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution.28Very_cheesy_and_sketch.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution(Very_cheesy_and_sketch)\">Solution(Very cheesy and sketch)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution(Very cheesy and sketch)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>First by the angle bisector theorem <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/6/19633cc23b004a8a1be1c57147c03f2958d25670.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BM=BD=\\frac{AB\\cdot BC}{AC+BC}=AB\\cdot \\frac{BC}{AB+AC}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"351\" height=\"41\" /> Similarly, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/d/6cdcf9397b70e4621d6af394f2d967d68cb28545.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CN=AC\\cdot \\frac{BC}{AB+AC}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"186\" height=\"41\" /> We thus have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a72f4226714ecbad687d4205ce9a12ec4bcb661.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AM=AB-AB\\cdot \\frac{BC}{AB+AC}=AB\\cdot \\frac{AB+AC-BC}{AB+AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"433\" height=\"41\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/a/7/ba7338aebe379fd4d334f14dc01171e7b51d0cec.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AN=AC-CN=AC\\cdot \\frac{AB+AC-BC}{AB+AC}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"341\" height=\"41\" /> Finally, since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/c/fdce8042980e5f1c094b2972601922081e3c6727.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,M,B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"65\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/4/c04adb52494e83ec3cda9949aef3dd2f83673b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,N,C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> are all collinear, there exists a homothety between triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/d/2edcdc0d73ef64ec441f60a3a8dccdbd10aa61a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BAC$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/c/7dcbd24f888801c82be1dd75b1cc4b0d7a160f0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$MAN$\" width=\"49\" height=\"13\" /> with scale factor <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/7/647cc59b95cf5caed1986ddb7d8aff07cb1db6a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{AB+AC-BC}{AB+AC}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"141\" height=\"41\" /> Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c7316a98db2988460043a4210657c967d03cb2ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC\\parallel MN,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"90\" height=\"20\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/5/dc509852d18c05b9b76d869e1461cce56d362a83.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{(C)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"43\" height=\"29\" />\n</p><p>--AndrewZhong2012--\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1975_AHSME_Problems/Problem_26&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017171849\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.013 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.022 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 128/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4606/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:20862:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017171849 and revision id 284557. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}